   were identified within protected areas compared to outside the areas.
   Overall, our findings revealed that residents and tourists perceive and
   appreciate the numerous CES arising from landscapes and seascapes of the
   island differently. This indicates a possible trade-off resulting from
   land or sea developments to the benefit among stakeholders, for example,
